==========================================================================
D. THE RETRIED LANE — is the data present, is it passed?
==========================================================================
  guard.py:511 call site kwargs -> NO retried kwarg
  guard.py:585 call site kwargs -> NO retried kwarg
  loop.py:185: tried: set[tuple[int, str]] = set()
  loop.py:323: at_str = f"{defect_file}:{s_}-{e_}"
  loop.py:331: at_str = f"{defect_file}:{obs.lineno}"
  loop.py:347: res.tried_log.append(
  loop.py:408: res.tried_log.append({"at": at_str,

  So: loop.py records every rejected candidate as '<file>:<lineno>' in result.tried_log, guard_once accumulates them
  into `attempts`, and neither rank_observations call site turns that
  into the `retried` set the law's veto lane reads.

  Does a second pass over the SAME file happen? guard.py:509-510 adds a
  file to full_sight ONLY when its packet was untruncated; guard.py:574
  skips only files in full_sight. A TRUNCATED pass-0 file is therefore
  re-ranked at guard.py:585 with retried=None.

  loop.repair()'s own dedupe set is per-call (loop.py:185), so the
  escalation pass re-tries pass-0 candidates and pays the suite runs
  again. Demonstrated below by construction:
    loop.py:185 -> tried: set[tuple[int, str]] = set()
